{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And she grabbed hold of his garment.</b> Midrash: were it not written about her, her hands would be forbidden [to touch] — her heart would be grabbing a person in the marketplace. For even among the most modest of the nations it is written here, ״ותתפשהו בבגדו לאמר שכבה עמי״. And she enticed him for twelve months, as it is said: ״ויהי כדברה אל יוסף יום יום״, and יום יום means nothing other than twelve months, as it is said: ״מיום ליום ומחדש לחדש״ — twelve. And when she would come to speak with him, he would lower his head and bury his face in the ground, so she made him an iron device under his chin so that he could not lower his head, as it is said: ״ענו בכבל רגלו ברזל באה נפשו״. She said to him: Why do you not listen to me? Am I not a married woman, and no person knows about us? He said to her: Even your unmarried women are forbidden to us — married women all the more so. Parable of a gentile who said to an Israelite: Come eat with me and I will feed you well, fat pork. He said to him: Empty one! Even your slaughtered meat is forbidden to us — pork all the more so. When she saw this, she said to him: If you do not listen to me, I will imprison you. He said to her: HaShem releases prisoners. She said: I will blind your eyes. He said to her: HaShem opens the blind. She said: I will cut down your height. He said: HaShem straightens the bent. She said: I will make you hated by all creatures. He said: HaShem loves the righteous. She said: I will sell you to a distant land. He said: HaShem guards strangers. When she saw this, she said to imprison him in the prison house. And were it not for the priests who judged him favorably, as I will explain in the chapter ויגש with the help of Heaven, they would have judged him in all these matters." "<b>And he fled and went outside.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: By the merit of ״וינס״, in your lifetime the sea will flee before your ark. This is what the verse says: ״הים ראה וינס״ — what did it see? The ark of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The phrase 'her hands would be forbidden' translates the cryptic לבה אסורים ידיה hyper-literally; the construction is textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:50.893165119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}